let's talk about paddling students on  the but kind of a weird topic for a  political show but it's what a school in  Georgia wants to do a school in Georgia  has sent out consent forms to parents  asking for permission to reinstate the  paddling of students on the rear end as  punishment there are many people who are  outraged but there are also parents in  the district who are pleased one-third  of the parents at this school reportedly  signing the consent forms so to  understand this story you have to  understand the term strict father  morality this is something I've talked  about on the program many times this is  something that exists among the right  which exposes that even though they care  to claim about policy they don't really  care about the best possible policy they  care about what feels fair to them or  what feels like justice to them and for  them justice usually means consequences  that feel good there's this phrase  that's become popularized I guess it's  been popularized by ben shapiro although  i'm not totally sure facts don't care  about your feelings it turns out that  for the right there approach is our  feelings are more important than the  facts so let me give you an example of  that and then i'll tell you how it  applies to the paddling of students in  georgia schools the right claims to be  against abortion and to want to reduce  the number of abortions they say to zero  that's great there's actually a lot of  people on the left and the right that  would agree on that let's reduce the  number of abortions to zero or as close  to zero as possible it happens that we  know how to do it comprar has  comprehensive sex education and no cost  access to contraceptives the right is  against that the right wants abortion  bans no sex ed and no access to  contraceptives why because a so-called  strict father would say if you have  non-procreative sex then you deserve to  get pregnant and if you do get pregnant  you deserve  to carry the baby to term 